  "component_type": "filter",
  "definition": "House money and reverse house money as one sizing modifier: the size moves with the unit's closed trades in R since an anchor.",
  "boundaries": "It reads only the cushion ledger the fold keeps from closed trades, so an open profit never presses. A fixed anchor (0) presses and brakes; a running-peak anchor (1) only brakes. Its role is `sizing_modifier`, so the compiler binds it in `/modifiers`.",
  "recognition": "The factor is 1 plus strength times the cushion over reach, never below 0, with the cushion and its anchor on the receipt.",
  "eligible_roles": [
    "sizing_modifier"
  ],
